+    "title": "Remote attach path: attacher, dispatch and status capability hooks",
+    "description": "Remote attach path (R1, R12, R16): attacher that finds or spawns the keeper via the rendezvous protocol and pumps stdio, the --x-mosh-* dispatch, host.rs hooks, and the status capability advertisement.\nSpec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session-design.md (§Keeper 'Socket path and lock' and 'Spawn', §Upstream touch list host.rs/status.rs rows, §Key abstractions Attacher/remote::dispatch).\nsrc/mosh/remote/{mod,attacher}.rs. remote::dispatch: closed match routing --x-mosh-session-v1 to the attacher and --x-mosh-keeper-v1 to the keeper entry point (keeper::run, filled by mosh-dqw.7; the arm calls it by name). Attacher, per the spec's rendezvous protocol: connect to mosh::keeper_socket_path(session); on ENOENT/ECONNREFUSED take the spawn lock, retry connect, then try the live lock non-blocking — acquired ⇒ no keeper alive: unlink the stale socket, release the live lock and spawn the keeper (current_exe [--session S] remote-client-bridge --x-mosh-keeper-v1 via detach_server_daemon_command + plain spawn, env_remove(SSH_AUTH_SOCK), not the launchd path), wait ≤5 s for the socket, connect; then pump with crate::platform::forward_remote_bridge_stdio(keeper_stream, false) unchanged. Upstream hooks: host.rs match arm `[o, ..] if o.starts_with(\"--x-mosh-\") =\u003e false, // mosh-fork hook`; host.rs `if let Some(result) = super::attach::mosh::remote::dispatch(args) { return result; } // mosh-fork hook` after the ssh-agent registration; status.rs pushes \"x-mosh-resume-bridge-v1\" into endpoint_capabilities on Unix (a fork test asserts it equals mosh::STATUS_CAPABILITY).\nowns: Attacher (fills attacher::run); owns: remote::dispatch; owns: x-mosh-resume-bridge-v1 capability advertisement\nconsumes: mosh constants and MoshConfig\nconsumes: keeper and attacher entry-point signatures; consumes: keeper rendezvous protocol (socket path, live lock, spawn lock); consumes: mosh module tree\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.1: consumes keeper rendezvous protocol and mosh module tree\nFiles: src/mosh/remote/mod.rs, src/mosh/remote/attacher.rs, src/remote/host.rs (2 hook lines), src/cli/status.rs (1 hook line)\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] Exactly 3 upstream lines changed, tagged; existing remote_attach tests pass; an unknown --x-mosh-* flag is an error, not silently accepted as plain.\n- [ ] In-process tests: stale socket file with no listener is recovered (unlinked, keeper spawn path taken); two concurrent attachers spawn at most one keeper (lock); a live keeper is connected to without spawning.\n- [ ] status client --json includes x-mosh-resume-bridge-v1 on Unix.",
