+    "title": "Configuration smoke: end-to-end resume tests over fake ssh",
+    "description": "End-to-end configuration smoke (R1-R13, R16, R17, R19): resume, stall, saved-machine health, grace expiry, multi-client, ghost eviction, live handoff, D6 late execution, and byte-identical fallback (no capability, kill switch).\nSpec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session-design.md (§Acceptance criteria, §Testing end-to-end).\ntests/mosh_resume.rs and tests/mosh_multi_client.rs drive the herdr binary with a fake ssh on PATH that runs the remote command locally (pattern tests/remote_attach.rs:69-107). Exercises each enumerated configuration: herdr --remote with a resume-capable remote; saved machine with a resume-capable remote; remote binary without the capability (plain fallback); HERDR_MOSH_RESUME=0 (plain).\nconsumes: mosh constants and MoshConfig (HERDR_MOSH_GRACE=5 for grace tests); consumes: Keeper; consumes: Attacher; consumes: LocalBridge; consumes: start_ui_bridge; consumes: local trace events; consumes: keeper trace events\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.7: consumes Keeper\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.10: consumes attacher, dispatch and status capability\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.8: consumes LocalBridge resume path\nFiles: tests/mosh_resume.rs, tests/mosh_multi_client.rs, tests/support (read-only reuse)\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] Kill the leg ssh mid-stream and mid-frame: keys before/during/after the outage reach the pane exactly once in order (pane content via tests/support screen helpers); HERDR_MOSH_TRACE shows welcome resumed and exactly one server_connect for the token (no reconnect snapshot). Saved-machine cases reuse the tests/machine_setup.rs fake-ssh pattern.\n- [ ] SIGSTOP the leg \u003e8 s: dead-leg detection and resume.\n- [ ] Saved machine outage \u003e10 s within grace: no health timeout, no supervisor reconnect.\n- [ ] Grace expiry: --remote exits with the reattach hint; saved machine takes the supervisor reconnect path; no hang.\n- [ ] Two clients: killing one leg leaves the other unaffected; the killed one resumes.\n- [ ] Client exit ends the keeper session within 2 s; a full reconnect evicts the previous token.\n- [ ] Live handoff delivers ServerShutdown (not ConnectionLost).\n- [ ] Idle healthy link: no traffic for \u003e8 s causes no leg replacement (trace shows no leg_down) (R17).\n- [ ] Keeper lifecycle (R16, R19): first attach spawns the keeper; a second attach reuses it; after kill -9 of the keeper the stale socket is recovered by the next attach; two concurrent first attaches spawn one keeper; the keeper exits ~30 s after its last session ends.\n- [ ] A request buffered past ENDPOINT_COMMAND_TIMEOUT executes exactly once on resume (D6).\n- [ ] Capability-less remote and HERDR_MOSH_RESUME=0 behave like upstream; tests/remote_attach.rs passes unchanged.",
