+    "id": "mosh-dqw.8",
+    "title": "Local bridge: resumable client pump and start_ui_bridge resume path",
+    "description": "Local bridge (R1-R7, R9, R10, R12): per-client resumable pump that keeps the client stream whole, buffers input through outages, injects status frames that keep saved-machine health alive and drive the banner, enforces the give-up deadline, delivers server-EOF frames then closes, and takes the plain path for kill switch, Windows remotes or no capability.\nSpec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session-design.md (§Local bridge behaviour, §Discovery and fallback step 4, §Session-end triggers, §Error handling summary, §Key abstractions LocalBridge/start_ui_bridge).\nsrc/mosh/local_bridge.rs plus the resume branch of start_ui_bridge in src/mosh/mod.rs. LocalBridge binds the user-facing socket with crate::ipc prepare_socket_path/bind_private_local_listener/restrict_socket_permissions (as start_command does at attach.rs:3038-3051), serves one connection at a time, keeps last_token for ghost eviction (previous_token in HELLO). Per connection: SessionEndpoint (8 MiB upstream ring), dial legs through the LegDialer, pump client↔session, forward only whole frames via FrameSplitter, keep accepting client writes during an outage up to the cap, inject LinkStatus Resuming every 1 s only after the first complete downstream frame and only between frames, inject Linked once after resume, give-up deadline = grace, poll should_stop ≤100 ms, session-end triggers (client EOF → END best effort; drop/stop; grace; overflow; unknown/ended), fatal leg class → failure_tx; Unsupported on leg 0 (nothing yet forwarded to the client) → serve that connection via upstream plain bridge_connection; Unsupported on a reconnect leg → end the session (outcome b). Any leg-0 failure before the first WELCOME new keeps today's semantics: no retry, failure_tx, close client socket; retry/back-off/give-up deadline apply only after the session exists. With HERDR_MOSH_TRACE=\u003cdir\u003e, append JSON lines to \u003cdir\u003e/local.jsonl for leg_up, leg_down{reason}, welcome{status}, resume{replayed_up,replayed_down}, session_end{reason}, inject{state}. start_ui_bridge returns an SshStdioBridge struct literal owning the thread, should_stop and failure_tx so reported_failure() and Drop keep their semantics; plain path when kill switch, Windows remote, or no capable candidate.\nowns: LocalBridge; owns: local trace events\nconsumes: mosh constants and MoshConfig\nconsumes: start_ui_bridge; consumes: SessionEndpoint; consumes: ReplayRing; consumes: FrameSplitter; consumes: link-frame injection encoding; consumes: LegDialer; consumes: SshLegDialer; consumes: LinkStatus\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.4: consumes SessionEndpoint\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.5: consumes FrameSplitter and encode_link_frame\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.6: consumes SshLegDialer and capability probe\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.2: consumes LinkStatus payload type\nFiles: src/mosh/local_bridge.rs, src/mosh/mod.rs\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] In-process tests with an in-memory LegDialer and fake keeper: leg killed mid-frame → client receives only whole frames, Resuming injections every ~1 s after Welcome, Linked after resume; no injection before the first frame; give-up deadline closes the client socket at a frame boundary; client writes accepted during outage; overflow ends session; Fatal → reported_failure(); Unsupported → plain fallback.\n- [ ] Kill switch, no-capability and Windows-remote paths return the plain SshStdioBridge (platform gate unit-tested in-process).\n- [ ] Leg-0 Unsupported serves plain; reconnect-leg Unsupported ends the session; leg-0 Retryable failure is not retried.\n- [ ] Input written by the client while no leg is up is buffered and delivered exactly once after resume (never dropped at the bridge); this plus server-side continuity is the whole D6 delivery mechanism (R11) — no request-level logic.\n- [ ] No upstream lines changed by this bead.",
