+    "title": "Keeper daemon: parked server sessions, drain and grace",
+    "description": "Remote keeper daemon (R1-R5, R7-R10, R16): parks the server connection per token across legs, drains while down, enforces grace, steals legs, evicts ghost sessions, and forwards server EOF/handoff as whole frames then END.\nSpec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session-design.md (§Keeper, §Ring caps and drain policy, §Session-end triggers, §Testing Observability, §Key abstractions Keeper).\nsrc/mosh/remote/keeper.rs: keeper::run entry point (invoked by remote::dispatch for --x-mosh-keeper-v1, owned by mosh-dqw.10). Takes the \u003csocket\u003e.live lock non-blocking for its whole lifetime (exits at once if another keeper holds it), then binds mosh::keeper_socket_path(session) 0600. Token table behind one lock; per session a LocalStream to client_socket_path(), a SessionEndpoint with a 16 MiB ring, current leg, grace deadline from HELLO.grace_ms (never from the remote environment; R18); fresh token → connect server, answer new; known → steal leg (close the old), answer resumed; unknown → unknown; previous_token evicted; drain policy (leg up + ring full → stop reading server; leg down → keep draining into ring; overflow ends session); grace expiry closes server stream; server EOF forwarded after the last complete frame (FrameSplitter) then END{server-eof}; idle exit 30 s after the table empties. The leg handler takes a plain duplex stream. With HERDR_MOSH_TRACE=\u003cdir\u003e, append JSON lines to \u003cdir\u003e/keeper.jsonl for welcome{status}, server_connect, leg_up, leg_down{reason}, session_end{reason}.\nowns: Keeper (fills keeper::run); owns: keeper trace events\nconsumes: mosh constants and MoshConfig\nconsumes: keeper and attacher entry-point signatures; consumes: SessionEndpoint; consumes: ReplayRing; consumes: FrameSplitter; consumes: keeper rendezvous protocol (socket path, live lock, spawn lock)\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.4: consumes SessionEndpoint and ReplayRing\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.5: consumes FrameSplitter\nFiles: src/mosh/remote/keeper.rs\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] In-process tests drive a keeper against a fake server socket: new/resumed/unknown/evict; leg steal closes the old leg; drain-while-down captures server output; overflow ends session; grace expiry closes server stream; server EOF delivered after the last complete frame then END; idle exit; second keeper exits when the live lock is held.\n- [ ] No upstream lines changed by this bead.",
