+    "description": "SSH leg dialer (R1, R2, R12, R13): capability probe and candidate re-selection, leg-0 vs reconnect-leg commands (reconnect: BatchMode, ControlMaster bypassed), back-off, and fatal/unsupported/retryable classification.\nSpec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session-design.md (§Legs, §Discovery and fallback steps 1-3, §Key abstractions Leg/LegDialer).\nsrc/mosh/ssh_leg.rs: SshLegDialer implementing LegDialer. Capability probe via remote_client_status for STATUS_CAPABILITY; candidate re-selection over remote_binary_candidates requiring the capability plus supports_endpoint_requirement (attach.rs:1519-1540,1588-1593); hint line naming HERDR_REMOTE_BINARY when none qualifies on --remote. Per-leg remote command from posix_remote_output_command + RemoteExecutable::command/session_args with [remote-client-bridge, --x-mosh-session-v1]. Leg 0 uses the same ssh options as today's path (interactive inherited stderr for --remote, noninteractive for saved); reconnect legs are BatchMode, piped stderr, ControlMaster bypassed (managed config: clone of ManagedSshOptions with control_path None; unmanaged: -o ControlPath=none via bridge_child). A Leg is one end of a socketpair whose other end is driven by upstream bridge_child (preamble stripping stays upstream's). Back-off 1,2,4,8,8… s, honouring caller deadline + stop flag. Classification (leg 0 on --remote has inherited stderr: classify from reported_failure() and exit status only; reconnect legs also use piped stderr): Fatal for auth failure, host-key failure, generation mismatch; Unsupported for 'unsupported remote client bridge option'; else Retryable.\nowns: SshLegDialer; owns: capability probe and candidate re-selection\nconsumes: mosh constants and MoshConfig\nconsumes: x-mosh-resume-bridge-v1 capability advertisement (an entry in upstream's endpoint_capabilities array of status client --json); consumes: Leg; consumes: LegDialer\nblocked-by mosh-dqw.1: consumes Leg and LegDialer interface\nFiles: src/mosh/ssh_leg.rs\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] In-process #[cfg(test)] tests (fake ssh technique of attach.rs:3684-3709): reconnect-leg command has BatchMode and no -S/ControlMaster (both managed and unmanaged config); leg-0 command equals today's; remote command contains --x-mosh-session-v1 and the session args.\n- [ ] Classification tests for each Fatal stderr sample, Unsupported, and Retryable; back-off schedule and stop/deadline honoured.\n- [ ] Probe/re-selection tests: capable first candidate; upstream-first candidate skipped for a capable later one; none capable → plain.",
