+    "description": "Inert compilable scaffold: mount line, mosh constants/MoshConfig (kill switch, grace), Leg/LegDialer/LegError, start_ui_bridge plain path with both UI call sites swapped (run_remote for --remote; connect_saved_ssh, the saved-machine supervisor connect path), and the keeper rendezvous protocol (socket path, live and spawn locks).\nSpec: docs/superpowers/runs/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session/2026-10-24-mosh-phase1-resumable-session-design.md (§Components, §Upstream touch list rows 1-3, §Key abstractions Leg/LegDialer/start_ui_bridge).\nCompilable scaffold that every other mosh bead fills in. Adds the single mount line in src/remote/attach.rs; creates src/mosh/mod.rs (constants STATUS_CAPABILITY=\"x-mosh-resume-bridge-v1\", flags --x-mosh-session-v1/--x-mosh-keeper-v1; env config read once: HERDR_MOSH_RESUME=0 kill switch, HERDR_MOSH_GRACE seconds default 60 clamped 5..=3600) and declares every submodule (session, ring, link_frames, ssh_leg, local_bridge, remote/{mod,attacher,keeper}) as compilable stub files; defines in ssh_leg.rs the transport-neutral Leg struct (duplex stream + teardown + failure report), the LegDialer trait and LegError {Retryable, Fatal, Unsupported}; defines start_ui_bridge(ssh, remote_herdr, local_socket, session, options, noninteractive, stop) -\u003e io::Result\u003cSshStdioBridge\u003e that for now delegates to SshStdioBridge::start unchanged (inert by default), and swaps the two UI call sites (attach.rs:90 in run_remote, saved.rs:35 in connect_saved_ssh) to call it. Also defines the keeper rendezvous protocol (spec §Keeper 'Rendezvous'): mosh::keeper_socket_path(session) plus the \u003csocket\u003e.live and \u003csocket\u003e.spawn lock paths and small helpers to take them: remote_bridge_endpoint_path with a short hashed name over (uid, session, session-protocol version, build id). Rendezvous rule: the attacher is a pure byte pipe (writes nothing of its own); the session protocol starts with HELLO end to end. Stub entry points keeper::run(args) and attacher::run(args) with fixed signatures (filled by mosh-dqw.7 and mosh-dqw.10). STATUS_CAPABILITY is advertised as one entry of upstream's existing endpoint_capabilities array in `status client --json`. Creates a placeholder remote::dispatch returning None (the abstraction itself is owned by mosh-dqw.10).\nowns: mosh module tree; owns: Leg; owns: LegDialer; owns: start_ui_bridge (sole owner; mosh-dqw.8 fills its resume branch); owns: keeper rendezvous protocol (socket path, live lock, spawn lock, pure-pipe rule); owns: keeper and attacher entry-point signatures; owns: mosh constants and MoshConfig\nFiles: src/remote/attach.rs (2 hook lines), src/remote/saved.rs (1), src/mosh/mod.rs, src/mosh/{session,ring,link_frames,ssh_leg,local_bridge}.rs, src/mosh/remote/{mod,attacher,keeper}.rs\nAcceptance:\n- [ ] cargo build and the full existing test suite pass; behaviour is byte-identical to upstream (start_ui_bridge always takes the plain path).\n- [ ] Exactly 3 upstream lines changed (mount + 2 swaps), each ending in // mosh-fork hook.\n- [ ] Leg, LegDialer, LegError and start_ui_bridge carry responsibility comments per the spec's Key abstractions entries.\n- [ ] Unit test: MoshConfig grace parsing clamps (unset→60, 1→5, 99999→3600, garbage→60) and kill switch.",
